/-
# Problem Description

Erdős Problem 144: is it true that almost all `n` have two divisors `d₁ < d₂` with
`d₂ < 2 * d₁`? `erdos_144` proves this is true.

Proved by Maier and Tenenbaum, who showed that almost every positive integer has two
divisors whose ratio is less than any prescribed constant greater than one; the file
specialises their result to the factor `2` asked for here.

`closeDivisorSet` is `{n | ∃ d₁ d₂, d₁ ∣ n ∧ d₂ ∣ n ∧ d₁ < d₂ ∧ d₂ < 2 * d₁}`, and
`Set.HasDensity 1` says the natural density of that set exists and equals one — i.e. the
integers with such a divisor pair have density one, which is "almost all `n`".
-/
